[anicel 0003] impeller/gles: stand again in an OpenGL context made anew

Board a-real-gpu-reset-went-unheard-on-the-main-pc, step two: the screen
comes back after a GPU reset without the app starting again. The embedder
makes a new OpenGL context; Impeller's ContextGLES is kept and stands on
into it.

- ReactorGLES::GLContextWasReplaced, called once the new context is
  current: every handle is stamped with the generation of the context it
  was named in, and one of a replaced generation names nothing and deletes
  nothing. The work waiting for the old context is let go of.
- A texture of the old context stands again empty, with a name of the new
  one; one that wraps another's object binds none and still binds (a pass
  whose textures do not bind ends the process).
- A buffer of the old context stands again whole: its bytes never left
  the backing store.
- The pipeline library forgets its pipelines and programs: a pipeline asked
  for from then on is linked anew.

